Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be even functions. That means $f(-x) = f(x)$ and $g(-x) = g(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$ and $g$, respectively.
We want to determine if $f(x) g(x)$ is even, odd, or neither.
We compute $f(-x) g(-x)$.
Since $f(-x) = f(x)$ and $g(-x) = g(x)$, we have $f(-x) g(-x) = f(x) g(x)$.
Now we check if $f(-x) g(-x) = f(x) g(x)$.
Since $f(-x) g(-x) = f(x) g(x)$, $f(x) g(x)$ is an even function.

