\begin{enumerate}
    \item First we need to find the prime factorization of 117 and 119.
    \item $117 = 3^2 \cdot 13$.  We can check this by dividing 117 by 3 repeatedly until we get a prime number.
    $117 \div 3 = 39$
    $39 \div 3 = 13$.  Since 13 is prime, we have $117 = 3^2 \cdot 13$. 
    \item Now we find the prime factorization of 119.
    $119 = 7 \cdot 17$.  We can check this by dividing 119 by 7 repeatedly until we get a prime number.
    $119 \div 7 = 17$.  Since 17 is prime, we have $119 = 7 \cdot 17$. 
    \item Then we find the prime factorization of $117 \cdot 119$.
    $117 \cdot 119 = (3^2 \cdot 13) \cdot (7 \cdot 17) = 3^2 \cdot 7 \cdot 13 \cdot 17$.
    \item The distinct prime factors are 3, 7, 13, and 17.  There are 4 distinct prime factors.
\end{enumerate}

