\begin{enumerate}
    \item Original volume: The original cube is 2 cm by 2 cm by 2 cm.  The volume is $2 \times 2 \times 2 = 8$ cubic centimeters.

    \item Increase in Volume: The volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters.  So the new volume is $8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters.

    \item New Cube's Edge Length: Let $s$ be the length of one edge of the new cube. The volume of the new cube is $s^3$. So we have $s^3 = 27$.

    \item Solve for $s$: Taking the cube root of both sides gives $s = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$ centimeters.
\end{enumerate}

